## Geometry Consequence
All six rows have edgeless dead-cover projections, but their E/branch gates do touch the singleton dead labels.  The obstruction is therefore not 'find a larger projection cut'; there is no edge to cut.
Every dead component is a singleton B0/B1 owner-pair component, and the exact interval mirror swaps the B0 and B1 owners.  The signed owner balance cancels row-by-row, so any useful current must be local to mirror pairs or touching gates rather than a raw global owner imbalance.
The finite terminal packet splits cleanly: rows 039 and 074 have minimum E/branch gates in the cover-delta sidecar packet, while rows 001, 062, 086, and 101 have branch-specific unit-delta minima.

